/**
 * Typed `{ event, code, payload }` envelopes for the host ↔ widget
 * `postMessage` channel.
 *
 * @remarks
 * The widget is a separate top-level browsing context running on
 * `onramp.arc.io`. It communicates with the embedding host strictly
 * through `postMessage`, never via shared globals. The envelope below
 * is the only wire contract that exists between the two.
 *
 * Two-tier vocabulary:
 *
 * - `event` (one of {@link ONRAMP_EVENT_TYPES}) describes the
 *   host-visible **effect**.
 * - `code` (one of {@link ONRAMP_EVENT_CODES}) describes the
 *   **cause** or sub-type. Each event maps to a closed set of valid
 *   codes — see the per-schema definitions below.
 *
 * Design rules:
 *
 * - Every payload is a plain object — no functions, no `Symbol`,
 *   nothing that survives `structuredClone` only by accident.
 * - `payload` is best-effort metadata. Hosts must branch on
 *   `(event, code)` first; payload fields are advisory.
 * - The widget never sends the session token back to the host: the
 *   token rides one-way on the launch URL only. Inbound `postMessage`
 *   payloads are *not* schema-filtered for token-shaped keys — the
 *   parser validates only that `event` is a non-empty string and
 *   forwards the rest verbatim. What makes inbound messages safe is the
 *   `event.source` + `event.origin` gating in `client/widget`, not a
 *   payload strip.
 *
 * The widget controller composes events on top of this envelope and
 * fans them out to host-registered callbacks (`onInitializationSuccess`
 * et al.). See `client/widget` for the dispatcher.
 *
 * @packageDocumentation
 */

/**
 * Base payload contract for every event envelope.
 *
 * @remarks
 * Payloads are intentionally open: the kit forwards whatever the widget
 * sends without asserting a closed shape, so additive fields from a
 * future widget release reach host callbacks untouched.
 */
type OnrampEventPayload = Readonly<Record<string, unknown>>;
/**
 * Payload fields the widget sends on every error envelope.
 *
 * @remarks
 * `errorMessage` (diagnostic copy) and `canRetry` (whether starting a
 * new session is worth attempting) are the documented fields. They are
 * typed as best-effort: the kit does not reject an envelope that omits
 * them, so treat them as possibly-absent at runtime. Any extra field is
 * forwarded untouched.
 */
